[[:db/cas 17592186056150 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186056151 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186056152 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186056153 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186056154 :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -9 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186056227 :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x = 1$ and $y =-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]$,\n$x = 1$ and $y =-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186056228 :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x = 1$ and $y =-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]$,\n$x = 1$ and $y =-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186056229 :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x = 7$ and $y =-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$,\n$x = 7$ and $y =-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186056230 :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x = 7$ and $y =-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]$,\n$x = 7$ and $y =-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186056231 :answer/value "$M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$,\n$x =-3$ and $y = 1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$,\n$x =-3$ and $y = 1$"] [:db/cas 17592186059584 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](images/ba/baf05a693deacc3ef644165bae4de7b1435a90c73f050ac76c48892b2e010393.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{array}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](images/ba/baf05a693deacc3ef644165bae4de7b1435a90c73f050ac76c48892b2e010393.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$"] [:db/cas 17592186059585 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/87/8773defc4db521e846b58b7c5ef04b54f26723d94099c75caffbeca0587c33dc.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n![](images/45/455dc49a531a371ea8aecd6259a677c8006bb2a23181ed66d27721135f240c89.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/87/8773defc4db521e846b58b7c5ef04b54f26723d94099c75caffbeca0587c33dc.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{array}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n![](images/45/455dc49a531a371ea8aecd6259a677c8006bb2a23181ed66d27721135f240c89.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$"] [:db/cas 17592186059965 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & -21 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -9 & -21 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186059970 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & 2x+4y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & 2x+4y=4.\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [:db/cas 17592186059970 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & y=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(2)=-8\\,⇒\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=2.$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & y=2,\\end{cases}$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(2)=-8\\,⇒\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=2.$"] [:db/cas 17592186059978 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 9 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n$M = \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 9 & 5\\end{array}\\right]$.\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [:db/cas 17592186060205 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186060205 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186060941 :tutorial/content "Consider the following system of linear equations and its respective **augmented matrix**:\n![](images/2c/2c5dfe046037750f98f773ad906094f5ffbad3c285adf200134a119f72888ac8.svg)\n\nIf we can convert the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form, then we can solve the system using back substitution.\n\nThe procedure for reducing $M$ to row echelon form using elementary row operations is called **Gaussian elimination**. To perform Gaussian elimination on a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, we use the following procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Consider the entry $a_{11}=2$ of the coefficient matrix. This entry is called a **pivot element**. We want to make this entry equal to $1$. So, the first elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Consider the entry $a_{21}=3$ below the first pivot element. We want to make this entry equal to $0$. So, the second elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_2 :=R_2+(-3)R_1\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Finally, consider the entry $a_{22}=-10$. This entry is the second pivot element, and we would like to make it equal to $1$. So, the third elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_2 :=\\dfrac{1}{-10}R_2\n$$\n\nand we get $M$ in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{-10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](images/b8/b83c4646349bada803311e5e9e160aafc8f08e6f51c7b69302def5ca4eeaa3fa.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3 \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = -1 \n\t\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\tx=\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left< \\dfrac{1}{2}, -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right>.$" "Consider the following system of linear equations and its respective **augmented matrix**:\n![](images/2c/2c5dfe046037750f98f773ad906094f5ffbad3c285adf200134a119f72888ac8.svg)\n\nIf we can convert the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form, then we can solve the system using back substitution.\n\nThe procedure for reducing $M$ to row echelon form using elementary row operations is called **Gaussian elimination**. To perform Gaussian elimination on a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, we use the following procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Consider the entry $a_{11}=2$ of the coefficient matrix. This entry is called a **pivot element**. We want to make this entry equal to $1$. So, the first elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{2}R_1\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{array}] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Consider the entry $a_{21}=3$ below the first pivot element. We want to make this entry equal to $0$. So, the second elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_2 :=R_2+(-3)R_1\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}{\\color{red}1} & 3 & -1 \\\\ {\\color{blue}3} & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+({\\color{blue}-3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}{\\color{red}1} & 3 & -1 \\\\ {\\color{blue}0} & -10 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Finally, consider the entry $a_{22}=-10$. This entry is the second pivot element, and we would like to make it equal to $1$. So, the third elementary row operation will be \n\n$$\nR_2 :=\\dfrac{1}{-10}R_2\n$$\n\nand we get $M$ in row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{red}-10} & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{{\\color{red}-10}}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & {\\color{red}1} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n![](images/b8/b83c4646349bada803311e5e9e160aafc8f08e6f51c7b69302def5ca4eeaa3fa.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+3 \\left( -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = -1 \n\t\\qquad\\Rightarrow\\qquad\n\tx=\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left< \\dfrac{1}{2}, -\\dfrac{1}{2} \\right>.$"] [:db/cas 17592186235879 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186235912 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186236215 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186236421 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186237357 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186237988 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186237988 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -\\frac{13}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{13}{2} & -\\frac{13}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{13}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186238272 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$"] [:db/cas 17592186238587 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{11}{16}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186238598 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186238787 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-4$ and $y=1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-4$ and $y=1$"] [:db/cas 17592186238893 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$"] [:db/cas 17592186239014 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{15}{16}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186239148 :