2186241137 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [:db/cas 17592186241137 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$"] [:db/cas 17592186241149 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186241149 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{13}{16}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186263066 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=-2$"] [:db/cas 17592186263833 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=13$ and $y=-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186263915 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=15$ and $y=1$"] [:db/cas 17592186263968 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=5$ and $y=-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186264512 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right],$ $\\,x=12$ and $y=2$"] [:db/cas 17592186266010 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [:db/cas 17592186266010 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+7y=-2 \\\\  & y=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x+7y=-2 \\\\  & y=-1,\\end{cases}$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+7(-1)=-2\\,⇒\\,x=-2+7=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5$ and $y=-1.$"] [:db/cas 17592186284851 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=12$ and $y=-3$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=12$ and $y=-3$"] [:db/cas 17592186285038 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186285062 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=0$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$"] [:db/cas 17592186285289 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-\\frac{17}{2}$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-\\frac{17}{2}$"] [:db/cas 17592186285438 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|