frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{20}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{5}{3}$"] [:db/cas 17592186286934 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=30$"] [:db/cas 17592186286951 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{9}{2}$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=-\\frac{9}{2}$"] [:db/cas 17592186286971 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186286994 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=0$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=0$"] [:db/cas 17592186287991 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [:db/cas 17592186287991 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & y=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -6 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & \\frac{10}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{5}{3}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x-2y=\\frac{10}{3} \\\\  & y=-\\frac{5}{3},\\end{cases}$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-\\frac{5}{3}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{5}{3})=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,x=\\frac{10}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}=0.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=0$ and $y=-\\frac{5}{3}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186287992 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix."] [:db/cas 17592186287992 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & y=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 1 & -2 & -4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x-3y=-\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & y=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{cases}$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{9}{2}\\,⇒\\,x=-\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}=-3.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-3$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186287994 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+8y=22 \\\\  & 7x-5y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & 3x+8y=22 \\\\  & 7x-5y=4.\\end{cases}$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186287994 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{71}{3} & -\\frac{142}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{3}{71}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 7 & -5 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{71}{3} & -\\frac{142}{3}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{3}{71}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{8}{3} & \\frac{22}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186287995 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & 3x+\\frac{1}{5}y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & 3x+\\frac{1}{5}y=9.\\end{cases}$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [:db/cas 17592186287995 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{4}{5} & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & y=30,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=30$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{1}{3}(30)=11\\,⇒\\,x=11-10=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=30.$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 3 & \\frac{1}{5} & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{4}{5} & -24\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{5}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{1}{3} & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 30\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\\begin{cases} & x+\\frac{1}{3}y=11 \\\\  & y=30,\\end{cases}$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=30$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+\\frac{1}{3}(30)=11\\,⇒\\,x=11-10=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$ and $y=30.$"] [:db/cas 17592186339149 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186339677 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186340461 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186340499 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186341077 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186342013 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+12y=-4 \\\\  & 5x+11y=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & 4x+12y=-4 \\\\  & 5x+11y=3.\\end{cases}$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186342013 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186386127 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186386127 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 8 & -16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 & 4 & -8\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 8 & -16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186386129 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186386130 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186386131 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186386132 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186386133 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{4}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388195 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186388195 :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186388197 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388198 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388199 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388200 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388201 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388202 :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+5y=-6 \\\\  & -6x-6y=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\\begin{cases} & 3x+5y=-6 \\\\  & -6x-6y=10.\\end{cases}$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [:db/cas 17592186388202 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186388204 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388205 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388206 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388207 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & \\frac{5}{3} & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186388208 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393299 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186393301 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393302 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393303 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393304 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393305 :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]"] [:db/cas 17592186393306 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=3 \\\\  & y=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-2)=3\\,⇒\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=-2.$" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -7 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y=3 \\\\  & y=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-2)=3\\,⇒\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=-2.$"] [:db/cas 17592186393308 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=-1$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=1$ and $y=-1$"] [:db/cas 17592186393309 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-1$ and $y=-2$"] [:db/cas 17592186393310 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=-5$ and $y=-4$" "$M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{array}\\right],$\n$\\,x=-5$ and $y=-4$"] [:db/cas 17592186393311 :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\